     "text": "MURRAY RODRIGUEZ AND PEREZ MEDICAL GROUP - DISCHARGE SUMMARY\n\nPatient: Cassandra Perry\nDOB: 09/28/1957\nSex: F\nMRN: 822109\n\nAdmit: 10/24/2009\nDischarge: 11/28/2024\n\nPrincipal diagnosis: Pancreatitis (chronic; cause alcohol)\nSecondary: None\n\nHospital course: The patient, Cassandra Perry, was admitted on October 24, 2009, with a diagnosis of chronic pancreatitis secondary to alcohol use. Over the course of her hospital stay, the patient's condition remained stable and she was managed conservatively with supportive care. There were no acute exacerbations or complications during her admission. The patient was educated on the importance of alcohol cessation and the management of her chronic condition. She was discharged home on November 28, 2024, in stable condition with instructions to follow up with her primary care physician and gastroenterologist for ongoing management of her pancreatitis.\n\nDischarge medications: None specific for pancreatitis. The patient was advised to continue any home medications as directed by her primary care physician.\n\nProcedures: None performed during this admission.\n\nSocial history: The patient reports current cigar use, approximately 6 times per year, which she started on February 19, 2012. She denies any current use of cigarettes or other tobacco products. The patient also reports consuming approximately 10 alcoholic drinks per week. There is a family history of hypertension in her father, who was diagnosed at age 70 and lived to age 88.\n\nLaboratory results: An outside lab result from Heritage Diagnostic Services dated October 22, 2012, showed the following:\n- Total cholesterol: 301 mg/dL\n- HDL cholesterol: 40 mg/dL\n- Fructosamine: 227 umol/L\n- Nicotine metabolite: Negative\n- Gamma-glutamyl transferase (GGT): 47 U/L\n\nVital signs during this admission were within normal limits, with a blood pressure of 132/70 mmHg and a weight of 130 pounds on November 28, 2024. Previous visit records indicate a blood pressure of 134/75 mmHg and a weight of 122 pounds on February 16, 2024, and a blood pressure of 139/74 mmHg and a weight of 135 pounds on May 6, 2023.\n\nPhysical examination: The patient's physical examination was unremarkable, with no acute distress noted. The abdomen was soft, non-tender, and without organomegaly. Bowel sounds were present and normal. There were no signs of acute inflammation or infection. The remainder of the physical examination was within normal limits.\n\nDischarge instructions: The patient was advised to follow a low-fat diet to help manage her pancreatitis. She was instructed to avoid alcohol completely to pr"
